  "result": "Perfect! The bulk discount feature is working correctly. Here's a summary:\n\n## Bulk Discount Implementation \u2713\n\n### Feature Details:\n- Lines with **10+ units** get an **extra 2.5% discount**\n- Applied **after** the line's own discount (or tier discount)\n- Both discounts counted in the `discount` field\n- VAT calculated on the amount after both discounts\n\n### Examples:\n1. **qty=9** (no bulk): Subtotal 90,000 \u2192 Discount 0 \u2192 VAT 18,900\n2. **qty=10** (with bulk): Subtotal 100,000 \u2192 Discount 2,500 (2.5% bulk) \u2192 VAT 20,475\n3. **qty=10 + 10% line discount**: Subtotal 100,000 \u2192 Discount 12,250 (10% line + 2.5% bulk on remainder) \u2192 VAT 18,428\n\n### Changes Made:\n1. **Updated `src/totals.js`** \u2014 Modified `invoiceTotals()` to:\n   - Calculate line discount first\n   - Check if qty \u2265 10\n   - Apply 2.5% bulk discount to the amount after line discount\n   - Include both discounts in total discount\n   - Calculate VAT on amount after both discounts\n\n2. **Updated existing tests** \u2014 Fixed 3 tests in `test/invoices.test.js` and `test/totals.test.js` that had lines with 100 units to account for bulk discount\n\n3. **Added 23 comprehensive bulk discount tests** covering:\n   - Bulk discount with various quantities (9, 10, 11, 100)\n   - Stacking with line discounts and tier discounts\n   - Multiple lines (mixed qualifying/non-qualifying)\n   - Edge cases and VAT calculations\n   - Interaction with vouchers\n\n### Test Results:\n\u2705 **438/438 tests pass** (415 original + 23 new bulk discount tests)",
